  "description": "meme-id: chocolate-melts-at-86f; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows a stack of chocolate bars melting, with the text overlay stating 'Chocolate melts at 86°F'. This is factually incorrect — dark chocolate melts at around 86°F (30°C), but milk chocolate melts at a lower temperature, and the melting point varies by composition. The meme's intent is to present a misleading or false scientific fact in a visually appealing way, potentially to provoke confusion or skepticism. While not explicitly abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful toward any group, it is harmful because it spreads misinformation, which can mislead viewers and undermine trust in factual knowledge. The intent is likely to create a humorous or ironic effect by juxtaposing a visually decadent image with a scientifically inaccurate claim, possibly to mock or highlight the absurdity of false information.",
